course: dictionary
lesson: 1078
title: Bowl: a dish, a roll, and a ground
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The words around it, its context, tell you which meaning is right. Look at «a bowl of rice»: the words «of rice» show that a bowl here is a dish of food, not a ball or a sports ground.
explain: Bowl can also be a verb, a doing word. To bowl is to roll a ball along the ground, as in bowling, or to throw the ball to the batter in cricket. Ask yourself: is the word naming a thing, or telling what someone is doing?
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning in place of the word and read it again. «The goldfish bowl» with the meaning round glass dish still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: A bowl is a round, deep dish for food like soup, cereal or fruit.
fact: A bowl can also mean the amount a bowl holds, as in «a bowl of rice».
fact: To bowl means to roll a ball, or to throw the ball to the batter in cricket.
fact: A bowl can be a round sports ground, like the Hollywood Bowl.
fact: One word can have several meanings, so always check the context.
exercise: «It reminds her of the goldfish bowl she upset last week.» What is a goldfish bowl? | A spoon for soup | A big plate for dinner | *A round, deep glass dish that holds a pet fish | A bag for shopping
exercise: «A 4,000-year-old bowl of millet noodles was found at Lajia in China.» What does «a bowl of» mean here? | A kind of ball game | A sports ground | A way of rolling a ball | *The amount a bowl holds
exercise: In cricket, what does to bowl mean? | To eat soup with a spoon | *To throw the ball to the batter | To run between the wickets to score | To wash a dish
test: Which of these is a sports ground shaped like a bowl? | *The Hollywood Bowl | A fruit bowl | A cereal bowl | A goldfish bowl
test: Which word is a verb in «Dad will bowl to me in the garden»? | Dad | *bowl | garden | me
exam: Ella says, «She put the apples in the fruit bowl.» In this sentence, what is a bowl? | A ball | A throw in cricket | A sports ground | *A round, deep dish
